From 722afda33f91618dd7f1b6e0b8f33e0b76a0bf16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bedirhan=20Gen=C3=A7aslan?=
 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:46:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/71] Shrink noisy tool output once its turn has finished

Most of a coding agent's context goes to command output, and most of that
output is progress noise: Compiling lines, per-test ok lines, npm's package
tree. What the model still needs afterwards is the summary at the end plus
enough of the head to recognize what ran.

Output from a finished turn is now reduced to its first five and last thirty
lines. This happens on the copy of history built for a request, so the
transcript and the UI keep the real output, and it happens at the same turn
boundary where reasoning already drops out, so it costs no additional prompt
cache invalidation.

Three guards bound the damage. Only successful commands are shrunk, because a
failure's output is the most valuable thing in the context. Only commands on
an allowlist are shrunk: a command we fail to recognize keeps its full output,
which merely costs tokens, whereas a command we wrongly shrink loses
information the model cannot get back. And a command line that chains, pipes,
or redirects is refused outright, since the output that matters comes from
what follows.

The replacement text names the exit status and says the harness did the
trimming, not the command, so the model does not mistake a shortened result
for a truncated one and run the command again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
